Z||000000||Viper||01-12-2000||01:29 AM||||Hi everyone!!!, the Viper man is back.!!<P>I'm the one that was going to look at the '88 4-cyl. coupe for 1,800 and 90,500 miles!<P>Well, I went today and checked it out, me and my dad went.  For an automatic it had a suprising amount of pickup (but then again, the only real cars I've driven are my mom's '89 Nissan Sentra (90hp) and a civic or two and a truck.  Well it was great!!<P>The body was in just perfect condition, it is white, I love the dent resistant panels!!  It was awesome!!<P>My dad got him down to 1,500!, not bad for a well running, great! looking Fiero coupe in the Silicon Valley on the west coast!<P>As a 16 yr. old, my insurance will only be $582 a yr!!, not half bad at all!! (liablility only)<P>Well, we closed the offer, and I'm handing the money over today, the whole thing has gone great so far!!, I love the fiero more than I thought I would ever!!, I still can't believe I'm gonna own a Fiero tommorrow!!!!! DAMN!!!!!!!!!!!!<P>1 Question: The Automatic Shifter, should there be lights to say if it's in Drive, or Reverse, or whatever?? Because I had to turn on the light to see them in the dark???, should there be lights there???<P>Thanks everyone!!, I'll let you know also when I finish the deal!!!<P>-Viper (Derek)||||reg||5
Z||000001||RossT||01-12-2000||01:39 AM||||Great score!  MAKE SURE YOU TAKE PICTURES!  You will remember this day as long as you live. Someday you will want to share your first car day with your kids.<P>congradulations.<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||01-12-2000||01:39 AM||||Let me be the first to congratulate you on your purchase.  I, myself, am partial to '88s, so I feel you got a great car at a great price and you will have a lot of fun with it.   <P>As for the auto shift thing....at night there is a light bulb that lights up to indicate what gear you're in.  It should also be easy to read in the daylight as there is a plastic thing under the console that is painted a bright orange color.  It is attached to the plastic trim and it may be broken.  Take the console off and take a look underneath to see if it's there or not.    <P>LMK if you need any help with it or have any other questions....I have owned 6 '88 Fieros (a coupe, 3 Formulas and 2 GT's) since 1990 and I know most of the car inside and out.<P>Congratulations again! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||01-12-2000||09:02 AM||||Congratulations, Viper!  You won't be sorry you did this.  You may have to iron out a few bugs early on, but once you get them solved, your 88 should give you years of faithful service.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroshop||01-12-2000||10:55 AM||||Viper,<BR>glad to hear you are getting your first car. The offer still stands you can bring the car to my shop and I'll check it out. Again congrats. and Ill talk to you soon.||||reg||7
Z||000005||fierospeeder||01-11-2000||11:29 PM||||I bought my fiero with the light out also.  I never found my parts store to carry that small of a light bulb.  And I always forgot to ask the dealer when i was there for other parts if they carried a bulb.  After a while you memorize the shift pattern.  P R N D 2 1 and be able shift at night.<P>This is your first fiero.  Good luck in traffic, there will be people trying to drag race you or tailgating you with their SUVs.||||reg||1
Z||000006||dogtired||01-12-2000||02:40 AM||||Saw your post earlier today?<BR>Checked when I got here and have already forgot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> the number <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>It was either a #74 or #84 and both AutoZone and ORilley's have them here in this great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> city?<BR>Its the same bulbs that are in your ash trays.<BR>Good Luck, Light em up!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000007||Scott2M4||01-12-2000||09:17 AM||||We have light bulbs in our ashtrays!!!???    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Viper||01-13-2000||01:11 AM||||Hey everyone!!!, Derek again!!, I got my Fiero!!!  I love the thing !!, it's great.................so I wonder still about  that bulb, I have a Kragen and Grand Auto around here.......and maybe the Fiero parts store or Fieroshp in Hayward has one!, I'm sure I'll find it........<P>Also, my light (pointed my way) the one activated by the button, is stuck, it's not on stuck, but stuck in there and off, it's kinda funky, I caused it after I got it.....it was already a little sticky.....anyway......sounds stupid, but how can I go about getting that top "console" where the lights are to take care of this??<P>Anyway, the Fiero is wonderful, it is the best looking Coupe or almost best looking Fiero I have ever seen....it's white with a spoiler.....it's just wonderful......<P>So help me out here, just trying to nail out a few dinks...<P>PS.  go the emergency blinkers working......and I love the gas tank opening mechanism,,,,,,,,,the Fiero is/was so ahead of it's time, it's amazing!!!<P>Later People!!  <P>-Viper (Derek)||||reg||10
Z||000009||dogtired||01-13-2000||04:18 PM||||The bulbs are P/N# 74. There are one in each ash tray and on the automatics one on/in the shifter indicator.<BR>Pull the ash trays out remove the 2 screws under each. Remove your shifter knob, on automatics there is what looks to be a big staple in the back, pull it out with a pair of needle nose pliers (don't loose it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  ) Manual shifters just un screw the knob.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Now you can lift the whole shifter surround up off the shift lever, on the automatics there will be the wires up to the shifter. 1/4 turn and you can see the bulbs. Also on the outside of each ashtray hole are the same bulbs/sockets, 1/4 turn and they are out. Its that easy???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Good Luck!||||reg||6
Z||000010||DRH||01-13-2000||04:59 PM||||Viper, congrats!!! Ohh to be 16 and buying my first car again...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The console light thing was a little hard to follow but it sounds like you are saying the on/off button for the overhead light pushed up into the housing??? <P>If so, pull the whole assembly out. There should be 4 screws holding it to the roof. I believe 2 are underneath the bulbs. Should either be phillips head or a small torx. The switch is held in place by a metal strip and melted plastic. More than likely the melted plastic broke loose. You may be able to re-melt it with a soldering iron. Just be careful not to melt thru and be aware it will make smoke (don't do it inside). <P>If it is unrepairable or you don't have the tools and/or inclination to do it, I would suggest getting in touch with Fieroshop to see if he has the whole assy. He is in your area and replied earlier in this thread. Click on the first icon that looks like a guy with a ? by it on his post to get his email.<P>Good luck, David. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||01-14-2000||04:26 AM||||T-15 torx for all 4 screws.  2 screws under the outer bulbs (reading lights) and 2 in the slots where the visors clip into.  If you can't fix yours and can't find another, I think (maybe) I know a boneyard where there are a couple cheap (might need to be painted).||||reg||1
